## Proposed Changes

### 1. Application Shell & Critical Paint

#### [MODIFY] [src/App.jsx](file:///c:/Users/mohamed%20imran/Desktop/nextal_academy%20-%20Copy/src/App.jsx)
- Remove `initialLoading`, `isFadingOut`, and the artificial `minDisplayTime` promise delay (800ms-1500ms) on initial mount.
- Remove the full-screen `<LoadingScreen />` overlay on initial mount, allowing the critical Header and Hero HTML/CSS to paint instantly.
- Dynamically import `@studio-freight/lenis` inside `useEffect` post-paint so Lenis does not inflate the critical bundle.
- Guard `ScrollTrigger.refresh()` in `MutationObserver` with debounce to prevent forced synchronous layout thrashing.

---

### 2. Render-Blocking CSS Optimization

#### [MODIFY] [index.html](file:///c:/Users/mohamed%20imran/Desktop/nextal_academy%20-%20Copy/index.html)
- Ensure critical variables, fonts, and above-the-fold layout styles (header + hero typography and grid) are present in the inline `<style>` block to guarantee zero Flash of Unstyled Content (FOUC).

#### [MODIFY] [vite.config.js](file:///c:/Users/mohamed%20imran/Desktop/nextal_academy%20-%20Copy/vite.config.js)
- Add a lightweight Vite build plugin (`nonBlockingCssPlugin`) using `transformIndexHtml` to convert the main stylesheet link to:
  ```html
  <link rel="preload" as="style" href="/assets/index-*.css" onload="this.onload=null;this.rel='stylesheet'">
  <noscript><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/index-*.css"></noscript>
  ```
  This eliminates the 150ms-1050ms render-blocking CSS delay without breaking any styling.

---

### 3. Intelligent 3D Scheduling & WebGL Lifecycle

#### [MODIFY] [src/components/Hero.jsx](file:///c:/Users/mohamed%20imran/Desktop/nextal_academy%20-%20Copy/src/components/Hero.jsx)
- Replace the 4000ms interaction-dependent delay with immediate post-paint scheduling:
  ```javascript
  useEffect(() => {
    let id;
    if ('requestIdleCallback' in window) {
      id = window.requestIdleCallback(() => setShouldLoad3D(true), { timeout: 800 });
    } else {
      id = setTimeout(() => setShouldLoad3D(true), 60);
    }
    return () => {
      if ('cancelIdleCallback' in window) window.cancelIdleCallback(id);
      else clearTimeout(id);
    };
  }, []);
  ```
- Result: Hero text and LCP paint first, then the 3D bundle immediately loads and paints the doll without unnecessary waiting.

#### [MODIFY] [src/components/HeroScene.jsx](file:///c:/Users/mohamed%20imran/Desktop/nextal_academy%20-%20Copy/src/components/HeroScene.jsx)
- Implement viewport and tab visibility observer:
  - Pause WebGL rendering (`frameloop={isVisible ? 'always' : 'never'}`) when hero is scrolled out of the viewport or when `document.visibilityState === 'hidden'`.
  - Resume rendering automatically when hero returns to view.
- Cap device pixel ratio: `dpr={Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio || 1, 1.5)}`.
- Add `stencil: false` to WebGL renderer parameters to save unnecessary GPU memory.

